{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy gives strong forward bias in clear space, uses one-shot recovery actions after obstacle events, keeps uncontrollable sensing total in every spec state, and reserves full_rotate only for a dedicated repeated-front-blocked last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in G",
    "Use specification states so each action state enables exactly one controllable action and obstacle events force recovery before exploration resumes",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward with occasional random_walk, while preventing repeated random_walk and repeated turn pulses",
    "Handle obstacle_left with rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right with rotate_counterclockwise consistently",
    "Handle obstacle_front through a dedicated backward escape, then short directed turns, and only after repeated front blockage allow a last-resort full_rotate"
  ],
